.UPDATE...
Issued at 1000 AM PDT Tue Aug 4 2026

Two updates to the forecast this morning:

1)Solid marine layer push this morning with ample coverage along
the coast. Despite the coverage it`s still rather compressed.
Compressed nature and topographic enhanced has yielded drizzle
here at the office in Monterey. The chance of drizzle will
decrease through 11 am as the marine layer clears back to the
coast.

2)Expanded today`s heat advisory to now include the Santa Clara
Valley and Santa Clara Eastern Hills. Upon further analysis and
fine tuning of temperatures HeatRisk coverage of Moderate to near
Major for Heat Advisory expansion. Keep in mind heat impacts can
be cumulative and today some of these locations have been over 90
degrees since Saturday.

