.SHORT TERM...
Issued at 148 AM PDT Tue Aug 4 2026
(Today and tonight)

The southerly surge of stratus that arrived earlier on Monday, has
allowed for stratus to become more widespread this morning. Nearly
all of our coastline has low clouds along it, with the stratus
penetrating inland. The Monterey Bay along with the majority of the
Salinas Valley has filled in, is slowly creeping into Bay Area.
Expect the marine layer to about 800-1000ft, which should keep high
temperatures for coastal communities and areas in or under the
marine layer reasonable. Clouds will begin retreating to the coast
by mid to late morning, leaving mainly clear skies across the
region. In terms of the upper level pattern, high pressure will
slowly take hold of the forecast. 850mb temperatures today, look to
to be between 24-29C, warmest across the interior. Expect
temperatures to a bit cooler than yesterday for areas influenced by
the marine layer, while other locations remain hot. Patchy Moderate
HeatRisk exists interior North Bay and interior Monterey, with areas
to widespread Moderate HeatRisk for interior East and South Bays.
Opted to hold off an issuing a Heat Advisory for these locations
tonight until we get a better visual on the marine layer expansion
since that could put interior temperatures at risk.

&&

.LONG TERM...
Issued at 148 AM PDT Tue Aug 4 2026
(Wednesday through Monday)

No major changes to the forecast as high pressure will continue to
build into the region and then hold through at least Saturday.
Temperatures will may decrease a more degrees on Wednesday, but it
will be dependent on the marine layer. Interior locations will still
be warm, but likely have temperatures in the 90s, perhaps cracking
100 in a few spots. Warmer and dryer weather starts to return on
Thursday as the ridge strengthens. Looking at models, 850mb temps
don`t really deviate too much. We`re still looking at that airmass
being warm, around 27-30C, depending on the model. Overnight lows
would be mild, especially in the thermal belts/mountains. And day
time highs would climb back into the 90s and low 100s. The HeatRisk
projection looks to have widespread Moderate HeatRisk for interior
slots, with pockets of Major HeatRisk. Heat Advisories may be
needed.

