.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1036 AM PDT Tue Aug 4 2026

MVFR-IFR stratus continues to clear out of the SF Bay and Monterey
Bay regions, and is expected to linger at the immediate coastal
regions. Gentle to moderate onshore winds are expected to develop
in the afternoon and evening with speeds of around 10 to 15 kt.
Stratus will return to the valleys tonight, with some more inland
expansion expected. Moderate confidence in stratus impacts at SJC
overnight into Wednesday morning. Smoke transport from fires
across the Pacific Northwest may result in impacts to slant
visibility due to hazy conditions.

Vicinity of SFO... Stratus has cleared out somewhat early as light
southerly flow impacted the terminal, with the winds turning to the
northwest this afternoon and evening, as speeds reach 10 to 15 kt.
MVFR-IFR stratus will return to the terminal region tonight, and
persist into Wednesday morning. Winds will turn more to the west and
the southwest at around 10 kt for Wednesday afternoon.

SFO Bridge Approach... Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals... SNS has scattered out to VFR, with VFR
conditions continuing through the afternoon. At MRY, IFR-MVFR
stratus continues through the morning with moderate to high
confidence that a brief period of VFR skies develops in the
afternoon and early evening hours. Moderate northwest winds will
develop in the afternoon and evening hours, becoming light
overnight as LIFR-IFR stratus returns to the region. Clearing of
the stratus is not expected until after the end of the TAF period.

